# Versions

The catalog is a tree of snapshots, like git without deltas. Uncommitted
work stays on **head** until Save. The UI word is **Save**, never Update.

## The rule

- **Shuffle, a new seed, or an explore tile** is a different planet.
  Saving it **branches**: a child of HEAD, even with no name.
- **Tilt, pins, genes on this seed** is the same planet. Saving it writes
  a newer generation of the current version.
- **A name** labels a branch when you want one. It is not what makes a
  branch. A nameless shuffle-save is still a branch.

Do not fold a new seed or explore draw into the current version. Do not
fork a new node for a knob move on the same seed. Explore likes may write
**ranges** to HEAD as they go; that is not a save of the planet.

## Language

**Save** — write the working planet. Same seed → this version, newer
generation. New planet → branch.
_Avoid_: Update

**Branch** — a child version. Automatic on shuffle / new seed / explore
tile; optional name is a label.
_Avoid_: Fork, copy, save as (unless naming)
